      "writtenOn": "2017-10-27T05:26:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The espi_vw_set_valid() function was removed,  and we also apply this change to espi_vw_set_wire().\n\nYes, we will have a race condition here.\nBut I think this is harmless and we can avoid interrupt being enabled unexpectedly.\neg: \na() dis-int\nb() dis-int\nb() en-int \n(interrupt already enabled here)\na() en-int.\n\nWe only have two interrupt mask settings and used to enable/disable CPU interrupt (enable\u003d0x4000fffc and disable\u003d0x40000000).\nIf interrupt is triggered in-between and come back to finish the sequence: The interrupt mask will be in enable state, and we will disable interrupt, do foo, and then restore it.",
      "parentUuid": "a864120b_588dbd88",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 89,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 95,
